WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.196 --> 00:00:03.431
The cookbook opens on its sections. Tap one to browse.

2
00:00:05.525 --> 00:00:08.758
Or search: suggestions appear as you type.

3
00:00:09.919 --> 00:00:13.165
Every recipe scales. Change the servings and every amount follows.

4
00:00:18.388 --> 00:00:21.627
Switch to US units, or tap a tinted amount to step through its units.

5
00:00:22.804 --> 00:00:25.235
Times in the method are timers. Tap one to start it.

6
00:00:26.345 --> 00:00:29.572
It keeps running at the top of the page while you move around.

7
00:00:31.827 --> 00:00:34.258
Keep a recipe in your favourites with one tap.

8
00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.927
Add its ingredients to the shopping list, at the servings you chose.

9
00:00:39.045 --> 00:00:42.263
The list is sorted by aisle. Tap an amount to change it, or tick it off.

10
00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.036
Ask the sous-chef about the recipe: swaps, timings, making it ahead.

11
00:00:47.153 --> 00:00:51.384
The answer appears as it is written.

12
00:00:52.587 --> 00:00:55.815
Share opens on the recipe card, ready to send with its link.

13
00:00:56.883 --> 00:00:59.510
Tick this to send the whole recipe as text with the card.

14
00:01:00.592 --> 00:01:04.226
Chat apps often drop words sent with a picture, so the text follows in one more tap.

15
00:01:09.019 --> 00:01:11.644
Print gives the whole recipe on A4, at your servings, with a code to open it.

16
00:01:11.723 --> 00:01:14.148
Tick the ingredients in pencil as you go.

17
00:01:15.414 --> 00:01:18.642
Add a recipe of your own. A title, the ingredients and the method are all it needs.

18
00:01:22.509 --> 00:01:24.942
Write the ingredients as on paper. Beside them, they read back as the recipe will.

19
00:01:29.129 --> 00:01:32.362
Write the method as you would say it: times and temperatures become timers.

20
00:01:33.452 --> 00:01:36.684
It is saved in this browser, ready to cook from. Export your recipes from Settings to keep a copy.
